       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose per administration:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. At this level there is a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily**, for 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours**, which is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest verifying it with pharmacy first, and I can add that to the order note."
      }
